## PYTHON RULES
- Always use type hints on every function parameter and return type
- Use Pydantic v2 syntax (model_config, not class Config)
- Use pydantic-settings for config (BaseSettings), not python-dotenv directly
- SQLAlchemy: use SessionLocal + Depends(get_db) pattern for all routes
- Never use async SQLAlchemy — use sync engine only (Celery workers need sync)
- All UUIDs use Python's uuid.uuid4() as default, PostgreSQL UUID type
- Always add created_at with server_default=func.now() on every model
- Never use print() — always use Python logging module
- Every service function must have a docstring
- Handle all exceptions explicitly — never bare except:

## FASTAPI RULES
- All routes use APIRouter with prefix and tags
- Always return Pydantic response models — never return raw dicts
- Use HTTPException with correct status codes (404, 422, 500)
- Include /health endpoint on the main app
- CORS enabled for localhost:5173 (Vite) and localhost:3000 (React Native)
- All file uploads use UploadFile from FastAPI

## DATABASE RULES
- Never alter tables manually — always use Alembic migrations
- After ANY model change: alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description"
- Always run: alembic upgrade head before testing
- Foreign keys always have ondelete="CASCADE" where appropriate
- Index frequently queried columns (campaign_id, status, gmail_thread_id)

## CELERY RULES
- Celery app defined in backend/workers/celery_app.py — import from there
- All tasks use @celery_app.task(bind=True, max_retries=3)
- Retry with exponential backoff: self.retry(countdown=60 * (2 ** self.request.retries))
- Always update job status in DB at start and end of every task
- Never import FastAPI app inside Celery tasks — use direct DB sessions

## ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
- All secrets come from .env via core/config.py Settings class
- Never hardcode API keys, passwords, or tokens anywhere
- If a new env var is needed, add it to BOTH .env.example and core/config.py

## BUSINESS LOGIC RULES — CRITICAL
- Daily email limit: 60 emails per day per campaign (hard limit, enforced in worker)
- Delay between sends: random between 30–90 seconds (never fixed delay)
- Max retry attempts per email job: 3
- Retry backoff: attempt 1 = 5min, attempt 2 = 30min, attempt 3 = dead
- Gmail thread ID must be saved after every send (needed for reply detection)
- Reply watcher runs every 300 seconds (5 minutes) via Celery Beat
- WhatsApp notification sent on: reply received, job dead, daily summary, campaign complete

## CLAUDE API RULES
- Always use model: claude-sonnet-4-20250514
- System prompt and user prompt are always separate (two-layer design)
- Output must always be JSON with keys: "subject" and "body"
- Parse Claude response safely — wrap in try/except, validate JSON keys exist
- If Claude returns invalid JSON, mark job as FAILED with reason "ai_parse_error"

## FRONTEND RULES (React)
- Use TailwindCSS utility classes only — no custom CSS files
- Support light mode AND dark mode (Tailwind dark: prefix)
- Components go in frontend-web/src/components/
- Pages go in frontend-web/src/pages/
- Use React Query (tanstack/react-query) for all API calls — no raw fetch in components
- Use React Router v6 for routing
- Use Axios instance (src/lib/axios.js) for all HTTP calls — base URL from env

## MOBILE RULES (React Native)
- Use Expo SDK 51+
- Navigation: React Navigation v6
- Styling: NativeWind (Tailwind for React Native)
- API calls: same Axios pattern as web, pointing to backend URL

## CODE QUALITY
- No TODO comments in generated code — either implement it or note it in README
- No unused imports
- No magic numbers — use constants or config values
- Every new file gets a docstring at the top explaining what it does
- Git commit messages follow: "feat:", "fix:", "chore:" prefixes

## VERIFICATION PATTERN
After generating any backend code, always show:
1. How to run it
2. What the expected output/response looks like
3. What to check if it fails

## WHAT NOT TO DO
- Never use Flask, Django, or any other backend framework
- Never use MongoDB or any NoSQL DB
- Never use SMTP directly — always Gmail API
- Never send all 100 emails at once — always through the queue
- Never store API keys in code
- Never skip Alembic — no Base.metadata.create_all() in production routes
- Never use synchronous sleep() in FastAPI routes — only in Celery workers
